[19:54:09] 🤖 IRIS:  To kill a Capybara subprocess, you would typically need to identify the specific process. Here’s how you can do it on different operating systems:

**For Windows:**
```shell
taskkill /F /IM capybara.exe
```

**For Linux/macOS:**
```shell
pkill -f capybara
```

If you're not sure about the exact process name, you might need to list all running processes first and then kill the specific one. Here’s how:

**For Linux/macOS:**
```shell
ps aux | grep capybara
```

This will show you the process ID (PID) of the Capybara subprocess. Then you can use:
```shell
kill -9 <PID>
```
Replace `<PID>` with the actual process ID.

Let me know if you need more detailed steps!
